{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato","soma"],"title":"Upasamā","html":"<article id='thig1.10'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Therīgāthā 1.10 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Verses of the Senior Nuns 1.10 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='soma'>Verses of the Elder Bhikkhunīs </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>Ekakanipāta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The Book of the Ones </span><span class='translation' data-translator='soma'>Chapter of the Ones </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Upasamātherīgāthā </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Upasamā </span><span class='translation' data-translator='soma'>Verses of the Elder Upasamā </span></h1></header>\n<blockquote class='gatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>“Upasame tare oghaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Upasamā, cross the flood, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='soma'>“Upasamā, pass over the flood, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>maccudheyyaṁ suduttaraṁ; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Death’s dominion so hard to pass. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='soma'>the sphere of death so difficult to cross. </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Dhārehi antimaṁ dehaṁ, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>When you have vanquished Māra and his legions, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='soma'>Carry your last body, </span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>jetvā māraṁ savāhinin”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>bear your final body. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='soma'>having conquered Māra and his army.” </span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>… Upasamā therī …. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span><span class='translation' data-translator='soma'>The Elder Upasamā </span></p></article>"}
